# Material UI TextField component

## slotProps API
Use `slotProps` prop instead of `inputProps` or `InputProps` props

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Material UI v6+
<TextField
  label='Street'
  slotProps={{
    input: {
      readOnly: true
    }
  }}
/>

// ❌ INCORRECT - Deprecated API
<TextField
  label='Street'
  InputProps={{
    readOnly: true,
  }}
/>
```

# Material UI Grid Component

## Grid API (Material UI v7+)
Use the `size` property instead of deprecated `xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg` properties:

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Material UI v7+
<Grid container spacing={2}>
  <Grid size={12}>
    <Item>Full width</Item>
  </Grid>
  <Grid size={{ xs: 6, md: 8 }}>
    <Item>Responsive</Item>
  </Grid>
</Grid>

// ❌ INCORRECT - Deprecated API
<Grid container spacing={2}>
  <Grid item xs={12}>
    <Item>Full width</Item>
  </Grid>
</Grid>
```

## Key Points
- Always use `size` property for responsive breakpoints
- Use `container` prop on parent Grid for layout
- example responsive values: `size={{ xs: 12, sm: 6, md: 4 }}`
- example single value: `size={12}`
